Run cat >/tmp/pr723-review.json <<'EOF'
{
  "event": "COMMENT",
  "body": "## Review Summary\n\n**Task:** @01KK7T2G3B8KMYSF48VJA1HAPA\n**Spec:** @session-branch-worktree\n\n### Own AC Coverage\n- [x] `ac-init` covered in `tests/session-branch-worktree.test.ts`\n- [x] `ac-commit-boundaries` covered in `tests/session-branch-lifecycle.test.ts` and `tests/session-branch-worktree.test.ts`\n- [x] `ac-sync` now has direct tests for `sessionBranchPull()` and `SessionSyncScheduler`\n- [x] `ac-status` covered in `tests/session-branch-worktree.test.ts`\n- [x] `ac-repair` covered in `tests/session-branch-worktree.test.ts`\n\n### Trait AC Coverage\n- [x] N/A — this spec does not inherit trait ACs\n\n### Code Quality\n- The daemon bootstrap still hardcodes the default shadow manifest path, so session sync is skipped for projects using a configured shadow directory instead of `.kspec/`.\n- Session branch sync/init still hardcode `origin`, so repos with non-`origin` tracking remotes do not satisfy `ac-sync`.\n- The full local regression gate is not clean: `npm test` currently fails in `tests/automation-eligibility.test.ts`, `tests/task-needs-work.test.ts`, and `tests/cli/session-start-notes.test.ts`.\n\n### Quality Gates\n- [ ] All tests pass locally (`npm test` failed: 3 test files / 3 tests)\n- [x] Own AC coverage reviewed\n- [x] Trait AC coverage reviewed (N/A)\n- [x] Code quality reviewed\n- [ ] Spec alignment verified — `ac-sync` is still incomplete for non-default manifest/remote configurations",
  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "packages/daemon/src/server.ts",
      "line": 457,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: This hardcodes the manifest path to `/.kspec/kynetic.yaml` instead of using the existing project-context loader. Repos with a configured shadow directory never enter session-branch sync here, so `ac-sync` is still broken outside the default layout."
    },
    {
      "path": "src/parser/session-branch.ts",
      "line": 576,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**MUST-FIX**: Session sync is still hardcoded to `origin`. `hasRemoteTracking()` only proves the branch tracks *some* remote; after that this fetch/ls-remote path ignores the actual tracked remote, so non-`origin` setups silently fail `ac-sync`. Match the shadow sync logic and resolve the configured/tracked remote instead of assuming `origin`."
    },
    {
      "path": "packages/daemon/src/server.ts",
      "line": 453,
      "side": "RIGHT",
      "body": "**SHOULD-FIX**: This scheduler is only created for `startupProjectPath`. The daemon already supports multiple registered projects, but additional projects never get periodic session-branch pulls, so their session state can drift from remote even while the startup project stays synced."
    }
  ]
}
EOF

